      "sentence_id": 25,
      "text": "7. The Tahsildar, Sattenapalli Mandal, Palnadu District.\n Respondents  Petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India is filed praying that in the circumstances stated in the affidavit filed therewith, the High Court may be pleased to issue any Writ, Order or Direction more particularly one in the nature of Writ of Mandamus declaring the action of the Respondent authorities in trying to acquire the Petitioners private properties being situated in Survey Nos. 148-B, 151, 220, 171-1C3, 423-2E, 423-2E1, 431-1C, 437-3A, 439-1A,\n439-1B, 439-1E, 442-1A1, 442-1C1 and 451-2A with an extent of Ac.30.38 cents at Nandigama Village, Sattenapalli Mandal, Palnadu District for the purpose of Widening/Extending to 4 lane on NH-167AG from KM 0.000 to KM 37.900 (Kondamodu - Perecherla Road) in the Palnadu District, in the State of Andhra Pradesh without paying due compensation as highly illegal, improper;\nunjust, arbitrary, against the principles of natural justice and against The National Highways Act, 1956 and in violation of Article 14, 21 and 300-A of the Constitution of India and order the Respondents to pay 3 times Of the present market value to the Petitioners for their extent of entitlements as mandated in The Right To Fair Compensation And Transparency In Land Acquisition,\nRehabilitationAnd ResettlementAct, 2013.",
